---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Join the lab" description="Open positions and how to apply to the Hinman Lab at UCLA Neurology.">
  <section class="border-b border-[color:var(--color-rule)]">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[color:var(--color-faint)]">Join</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-serif text-4xl tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Open positions</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
        We recruit at all career stages — postdoctoral fellows, staff research associates, graduate
        students, and UCLA undergraduates. We're committed to equity in education, science, and
        medicine.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-12 sm:px-8 sm:py-16 space-y-12">
      <article class="border-t border-[color:var(--color-ink)] pt-6">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl tracking-tight">Postdoctoral Fellow — Intracranial Atherosclerosis (ICAD)</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          Drs. Jason Hinman (Neurology), David Liebeskind (Neurology), and Naoki Kaneko (Radiology) are
          co-hosting a postdoctoral fellowship to study cerebrovascular biology in the context of
          intracranial atherosclerosis (ICAD). Using data and models of patient-specific ICAD lesions
          — the leading worldwide cause of stroke — the project aims to identify biologic pathways
          that promote localized thrombosis.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          The fellow will develop expertise in ICAD pathogenesis, 3D printing, endothelial cell
          biology, spatial transcriptomics, gene expression, and advanced light microscopy. Two-year
          appointment, NIH-funded.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="border-t border-[color:var(--color-rule)] pt-6">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl tracking-tight">Postdoctoral Fellow — Stroke &amp; Tau</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          Two-year position to study molecular pathways activated by stroke that regulate tau
          aggregation in a model of mixed vascular and Alzheimer's dementia. Includes testing of new
          chemical entities to block stroke-activated enzymes (Mark4).
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="border-t border-[color:var(--color-rule)] pt-6">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl tracking-tight">Staff Research Associate</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          Multiple open SRA positions to work on human biomarker studies as part of NIH-funded
          projects focused on vascular cognitive impairment. Background in immunoassays and proteomics
          preferred.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="border-t border-[color:var(--color-rule)] pt-6">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl tracking-tight">UCLA Undergraduate Volunteers</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          UCLA undergraduates interested in research opportunities in the lab should fill out the
          following intake form.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <a
            href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc2fHkRVUrUNckaJTPawdSIynf0Q7xdNKA5P-1EBk_70JUmJw/viewform"
            class="inline-flex items-center rounded-md bg-[color:var(--color-accent)] px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-white no-underline hover:bg-[color:var(--color-accent-hover)]"
            rel="external noopener"
          >
            Undergraduate interest form →
          </a>
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="border-t border-[color:var(--color-rule)] pt-6">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl tracking-tight">How to apply</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          For postdoctoral and staff inquiries, email Dr. Hinman with (1) a cover letter describing
          your research interests and which project(s) align with your goals, (2) your CV, and
          (3) contact information for three references.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <a href="/contact/" class="no-underline">Contact information →</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
